From 97ec637e75255e2d8ba370808a570a95fb87e27a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:39:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 110/110] Shutdown, server log and control panel

Stopping the server saves everything in time on a busy universe:
items are saved 2,000 rows to a statement (one statement went over
MySQL's max_allowed_packet and nothing was saved), item attributes are
saved in bulk too, the log says how long the item save and the whole
shutdown took, and Docker's stop_grace_period is ten minutes (the stop
still ends as soon as the server has exited).

The server's log file, one per start, is mapped out of the container
to ./logs (see logs/README.txt), and a release build flushes it at most
a second behind the console and line by line once the server is
stopping.

Fixes rolled in:
- clients leave their fleets, and their station's guest list, when the
  server halts
- the control panel starts the server again when Docker trips over
  replacing its container, and its Stop says the save can take a few
  minutes
